<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hurricane Maria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2017">2017</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hurricane Maria was a Category 5 hurricane that struck the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> in September 2017, two weeks after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-irma">Hurricane Irma</a>. It caused catastrophic damage on Dominica and then crossed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, destroying its power grid; studies estimated around 3,000 deaths there in the following months. It is among the deadliest Atlantic hurricanes of modern times.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-maria.jpg" alt="Hurricane Maria" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Worldview · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maria_2017-09-20_0238Z_(Coastline-less).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
